Changes made
------------
1. Multiple enzymes
   digest_sequence() and get_concatemer_seqs() take a list of enzymes instead
   of one. Cut points are the sorted union of each enzyme's sites, de-duplicated
   (a position cut by two enzymes is one cut in the tube).

2. Version-independent site location  [src/pore_c_aqb/sites.py, new]
   Bio.Restriction.search() changed its answer at sequence boundaries between
   biopython 1.82 and 1.88, making the digest irreproducible across
   environments. Sites of palindromic enzymes are now located here under one
   documented rule. Non-palindromic (Type IIS) enzymes are still delegated to
   Biopython.

3. Enzyme validation  [src/pore_c_aqb/enzymes.py, new]
   All names are resolved and checked before any read is processed, with
   close-match suggestions on typos. Isoschizomers (DpnII/MboI) are collapsed.
   Enzymes that cut twice, or have no defined cut position, are rejected.

4. Per-enzyme cut statistics  [DigestStats]
   Reports how many cuts each enzyme contributed, so a failed enzyme is visible
   immediately. Written to stderr and, with --stats, to TSV.

5. Provenance
   A @PG line recording the tool, version, command line and enzyme list is
   added to the output BAM header.

6. Command-line interface  [src/pore_c_aqb/cli.py, new]
   Argument-compatible with `pore-c-py digest`; adds --stats and --dry-run.
